// A HOST-AUTHENTICATED TRANSPORT: a transport already bound (by gunbc.host.host_bound_transport) to the
// managed host its ADDRESS reaches, checked additionally against a TRUSTED STATEMENT of the key that host
// presents. The binding is GENERIC -- host plus anchor gives a binding -- and each anchored machine lives
// in a ROW below, never in a module or a branch of its own (§3: one place for the mechanism, rows for
// the machines).
//
// WHY IT EXISTS. host_bound_transport_of binds a transport to the managed host its address reaches --
// read through the same route a FleetSsh target is built by, so a transport to one machine can never be
// labelled another. What it does not do is verify the SERVER: a target resolved for a host completes a
// TCP session with whatever answers at that address. A host-authenticated transport adds the check that
// notices -- the key the host PRESENTS must equal a trusted statement about this machine, written in the
// enrollment registry's own carrier (gunbc.fleet.fleet_host_key_enrollment KnownHostKeyRow; inhabited,
// no parallel row type).
//
// THE ONE ANCHORED MACHINE TODAY IS mtcollins1, and it is a ROW (mtcollins1_anchored_host_row). Its
// operator ruling (2026-10-22, option A): mtcollins1 is diskless -- a gunbc.runner.runner_host_medium
// RAM image -- and its SSH host key is a STABLE key delivered on every boot. The private half is a Secret
// in the fleet secret store beside the gunbai-ci App key (gunbc.auth.gcp_secret_access
// fleet_secrets_gcp_project; the ref is gunbc.fleet.fleet_ssh_access mtcollins1_ssh_host_key_secret), and
// under rule Q1 it lives in memory on the host only: never on disk across boot, never committed, never in
// argv, never logged. Its delivery route is the ONE route that already pushes the App credential per boot
// (gunbc.design_ruling mtcollins1_in_memory_app_credential_per_boot): the credential arm
// gunbc.fleet.host_credential_custody_converge Mtcollins1SshHostKey -- a new ARM on the existing custody
// route, keyed on the ROW, carrying the key to a tmpfs path at owner-read mode under the same custody.
// NOT a fork of the route. Booting mtcollins1 is ruled not sensitive.

// ── 1. The rows: one per anchored machine, the machine's name lives HERE and nowhere else ─────────

// WHAT IS ANCHORED: a managed host, the trusted statement about the key it presents (Absent until that
// statement is authored -- see mtcollins1's row), the read obligation the statement carries as a VALUE,
// the Secret holding the private half (so the scan's argv check can assert the name never renders), and
// the address the statement is stated at, built by the registry's own constructor so the anchor, the scan
// and the registry cannot spell one endpoint twice (§3).
type AnchoredHostRow {
  host: HostIdentity
  anchor: KnownHostKeyRow?
  read_obligation: NonEmptyStr
  host_key_secret: SecretRef
  address: SocketAddress
}

// THE ANCHORED HOSTS. mtcollins1's row is the only entry today; adding a second anchored machine adds a
// ROW here, not a module and not a branch.
data anchored_hosts: List<AnchoredHostRow> = [mtcollins1_anchored_host_row]

// THE READ OBLIGATION mtcollins1's anchor carries as a value. The anchor is authored by transcribing the
// PUBLIC half of a private key held on the far side of Secret Manager -- a figure copied across a
// boundary nothing in the DAG can read back -- so its standing is TranscribedUncited, and the obligation
// names the read that discharges it: a live boot's PRESENTED key, scanned at sshd's standard port and
// matched line for line. Until that match executes, the anchor grounds refusals; no transport seated on
// an un-matched anchor may carry real traffic. The scan also inherits the pairing obligation #14738 left
// open (gunbc.runner.runner_lost_boot_sweep_plan lost_boot_sweep_effect_pairing_frontier): a boot is not
// a boot until the minted evidence is recorded through the real dispatch. The live boot and the scan are
// GATED on merry-fox-82's go relayed by snappy-koi-83; nothing here runs live on its own.
data mtcollins1_host_key_read_obligation: NonEmptyStr = concat("scan mtcollins1 at sshd's standard port on a live boot (this module's anchored_host_key_scan_wet, GATED) and match the presented key against the anchor row; the private half lives in Secret Manager (secret name ", concat(mtcollins1_ssh_host_key_secret.secret as String, ") and only the public half is transcribed, so an un-matched row is a figure nobody read back. Discharging this also discharges the scan's share of gunbc.runner.runner_lost_boot_sweep_plan lost_boot_sweep_effect_pairing_frontier: the minted evidence must be recorded through the real dispatch. The live boot and scan wait on merry-fox-82's go, relayed by snappy-koi-83.")) as NonEmptyStr

// MTCOLLINS1'S ROW. THE ANCHOR IS ABSENT AND THAT IS THE HONEST STATE, not an omission: the stable key
// has not been generated, and generating it plus writing it into Secret Manager is a PRIVILEGED EFFECT
// (secretmanager create + addVersion on the fleet store) belonging to the operator or merry-fox-82 --
// this module prepares the command and refuses to invent the result. Fabricating a public half (DESIGN
// 4d: no value without an observation behind it) would mint an anchor able to accept a wrong key forever,
// the exact defect an anchor exists to close. So production reads an absent anchor today, and every
// transport ROUTED through anchored_host_transport_of refuses at AnchoredBindingAnchorAbsent (the
// witness pins that). Production folds do not route through it yet -- that gap is carried by
// anchored_host_transport_frontier_rows with its trigger, not hidden here. When the key exists, the
// transcription lands here as Present { value: anchored_host_trusted_row(...) } -- through the admitted
// mint (gunbc.host.mtcollins1_ssh_host_key_mint, whose receipt names the public half and the fingerprint
// together), which is the only door and makes the standing unskippable.
data mtcollins1_anchored_host_row: AnchoredHostRow = AnchoredHostRow {
  host: operator_host_mtcollins1,
  anchor: mtcollins1_host_key_anchor(),
  read_obligation: mtcollins1_host_key_read_obligation,
  host_key_secret: mtcollins1_ssh_host_key_secret,
  address: fleet_name_at_ssh_port(labels: ["mtcollins1" as DnsLabel]),
}

// mtcollins1's anchor. THE VALUE IS ABSENT AND THAT IS THE HONEST STATE (the note above the row): the
// stable key is not minted yet; when it is, the transcription lands here as
// Present { value: anchored_host_trusted_row(...) } with the public half and fingerprint read off the
// minted key -- through the admitted mint (gunbc.host.mtcollins1_ssh_host_key_mint), which is the only door
// and makes the standing unskippable. THE ANCHOR IS FILLED FROM THE MINT'S RECEIPT AND NOT FROM THE
// TRANSPORT'S OWN MEMORY: the mint reads this call to decide whether a key already exists, so a row that
// named a key the store did not have would silence the only thing that could ever create one.
fn mtcollins1_host_key_anchor() -> KnownHostKeyRow? {
  none
}

// The row a host is anchored by, if any. Absent for a host that is not anchored at all -- which is a
// refusal below, not a fallback: matching against nothing is accepting anything.
fn anchored_host_row_for(host: HostIdentity) -> AnchoredHostRow? {
  fold(anchored_hosts, init: none, f: fn(acc, row) {
    match acc {
      Present { value: _ } => acc
      Absent => if host_identity_eq(a: row.host, b: host) { Present { value: row } } else { none }
    }
  })
}

// THE ONE MINT OF A TRUSTED STATEMENT. Admitted to the row's anchor above and to this module's witness:
// a row built beside this call carries no standing, and a row built here cannot drop one. It takes the
// row's COMPONENTS, not the row itself, so a row's anchor can be built from its own host/address/
// secret without a value cycle.
//
// THE ARM IS ScannedFirstContact, DELIBERATELY -- and the registry itself sets that rule. Its comment
// (gunbc.fleet.fleet_host_key_enrollment, the srv5/srv6 note) says a row whose external corroboration
// EXISTS BUT WHOSE JOIN HAS NOT BEEN PERFORMED stays ScannedFirstContact, because IndependentlyAnchored
// "would be a claim about work that has not happened -- the same over-claim in a different place" (and
// DESIGN §4d forbids asserting as deduced what is only inferred). This anchor's join -- matching the
// transcribed public half against a live boot's PRESENTED key -- has not executed, so the row carries the
// measured, honest arm: scanned_from records the method (transcription of the minted public half, never
// read back) and the TranscribedUncited standing beside its read obligation, so both are visible to any
// reader of the row. The flip to IndependentlyAnchored { authority } belongs to whoever EXECUTES the
// readback match and cites the receipt -- the same un-widened flip the registry leaves ready for the
// Spark units. The row still anchors refusals today; what it may not do is claim a corroboration that
// has not happened.
fn anchored_host_trusted_row(
  host: HostIdentity,
  address: SocketAddress,
  host_key_secret: SecretRef,
  read_obligation: NonEmptyStr,
  public_key_base64: String,
  sha256_fingerprint: String,
) -> KnownHostKeyRow
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.host.anchored_host_transport", decl_name: "mtcollins1_host_key_anchor"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.host.anchored_host_transport_witness", decl_name: "anchored_fixture_row"),
  ]
  = KnownHostKeyRow {
    host: host,
    address: address,
    key_type: "ssh-ed25519",
    public_key_base64: public_key_base64,
    sha256_fingerprint: sha256_fingerprint,
    provenance: ScannedFirstContact {
      scanned_from: join([
        "transcription (never read back) of the public half of the Secret Manager stable host key ",
        host_key_secret.secret as String,
        " (project ", host_key_secret.project as String,
        "); standing TranscribedUncited until the readback match executes; read obligation: ",
        read_obligation as String,
      ], ""),
    },
  }

// ── 2. The binding: host_bound_transport_of first, then the host's own trust tests ────────────────

// §3c: the anchored binding and the gated readback are CONSUMED BY A NAMED LATER CHANGE, not dangling and
// not consumed-in-this-change (review 85051, correctly): no production fold yet routes a FleetSsh transport
// to mtcollins1 through anchored_host_transport_of, and nothing starts sshd pointing at the delivered key --
// the RAM image has no sshd in this slice at all (gunbc.runner.runner_host_first_boot_receipt
// unobserved_after_first_boot: "no network or sshd exists in this slice"). These rows state that honestly
// with the trigger that retires each, and they stand in the census-closure registry
// (gunbc.census_closure_frontier); this module's witness pins they are well-formed and registered (the
// network_boot_manifest_broker pattern). Until they dissolve, production transports to mtcollins1 do NOT
// pass through this module, and the honest claim is only: any transport ROUTED through
// anchored_host_transport_of refuses at AnchoredBindingAnchorAbsent today -- not that every production
// transport does.
data anchored_host_transport_frontier_rows: List<FrontierRow> = [
  frontier_row_decl(
    ref: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.host.anchored_host_transport", decl_name: "anchored_host_transport_of"),
    reason: "anchored_host_transport_of is called only by this module's witness and by anchored_host_transport_against; no production fold routes a FleetSsh transport to an anchored host through it, so no live transport is host-authenticated yet and unanchored binding through host_bound_transport_of remains the only production path",
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(
      description: "dissolves when a production fold that sends traffic to an anchored host calls anchored_host_transport_of with that host's FleetSsh transport and the presented line from a live readback, and refuses the leg on any non-Bound arm; a witness claim does not fire this"
    )
  ),
  frontier_row_decl(
    ref: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.host.anchored_host_transport", decl_name: "anchored_host_transport_per_boot"),
    reason: "anchored_host_transport_per_boot and per_boot_pin_from_console_line are called by this module's witness and, as the proposal, by gunbc.runner.runner_host_medium runner_host_key_observation (which supplies the boot id from the bound capture envelope) and anchored_host_transport_live_per_boot; no production fold holds a host capture and calls that live route (runner_qualification_attempt_run calls anchored_host_transport_live with the static anchor)",
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(
      description: "dissolves when a production fold acting on a mtcollins1 boot reads that boot's SOL console, parses its key line with per_boot_pin_from_console_line, supplies the subject's boot id as expected_boot_id, and refuses the leg on any non-Bound arm from anchored_host_transport_per_boot; a witness claim does not fire this"
    )
  ),
  frontier_row_decl(
    ref: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.host.anchored_host_transport", decl_name: "per_boot_console_marker"),
    reason: "the console-line grammar (GUNBC-HOST-KEY boot_id=<id> ssh-ed25519 <base64> SHA256:<fingerprint>) now has a producer, the runner-medium stages host-key-privsep, host-key-gen, host-key-pub, host-key-fingerprint and host-key-sshd, but the pairing obligation is open: the witness renders the stage commands and composes the line from SUPPLIED section bodies, and no execution of the rendered stage on a real or emulated boot has shown it emits exactly this shape; the fleet public key is also not yet seeded as authorized_keys",
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(
      description: "dissolves when a claim executes the rendered host-key stages on a real or emulated boot of the medium and the captured line parses through per_boot_pin_from_console_line, and an authorized_keys seed for the fleet public key is declared on the medium; the line shape in this module is then derived from that stage, not retyped"
    )
  ),
  frontier_row_decl(
    ref: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.host.anchored_host_transport", decl_name: "anchored_host_key_scan_wet"),
    reason: "the gated readback is prepared and GATED: it is called only by the witness (wet arms never execute) and no workflow dispatches it, so no presented key has ever been read back and every production anchor stays Absent",
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(
      description: "dissolves when, on a live boot of mtcollins1 with merry-fox-82's relayed go, this wet arm executes its Present branch over the real transport and the printed presented line is recorded through the real dispatch (lost_boot_sweep_effect_pairing_frontier) and transcribed into the anchor through anchored_host_trusted_row; a simulated Present does not fire this"
    )
  ),
  frontier_row_decl(
    ref: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.host_credential_custody_converge", decl_name: "host_credential_custody_row"),
    reason: "the Mtcollins1SshHostKey arm delivers /run/gunbc-ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key under custody, but nothing in this diff consumes the placed file: the RAM image has no sshd in this slice (gunbc.runner.runner_host_first_boot_receipt unobserved_after_first_boot), so the delivery is the precondition of a consumer, not its proof",
    dissolution: unbound_dissolution(
      description: "dissolves when the boot route for mtcollins1 starts sshd with HostKey pointing at exactly the custody-placed path and a live boot's presented key is read back and matched (the read obligation on this module's anchor row); a placement receipt alone does not fire this"
    )
  ),
  // THE MINT SHELL'S TRAP BODY, WHICH NO LONGER EXISTS (2026-10-28). This row registered the mint's trap as
  // a declared residual -- a single string literal, the '; '-joined cleanup commands passed as the trap's one
  // quoted word, because the bash fold grammar had no node production that renders a compound body bare -- and
  // its trigger named the capability that would retire it (a compound-body arm for trap). The trigger fired by
  // a route the row did not anticipate: rather than the trap gaining a node production, the MINT stopped being a
  // shell script at all. The private half's cleanup is now performed by the run itself -- the generation
  // removes its own create-only directory on every path out, and reports a refusal that could not (
  // gunbc.host.fleet_keypair_mint fleet_keypair_generate_pair) -- so there is no trap, no emitted script, and
  // no literal left to dissolve. Deleting the row is the honest act: a frontier row whose decl no longer exists
  // would not resolve, and a row kept to preserve an audit trail belongs in the retirement note at the foot of
  // this module rather than in a registry that asserts a live residual.
]

type AnchoredHostBinding
  = AnchoredBindingBound { bound: HostBoundTransport }
  | AnchoredBindingNotTheAnchoredHost { cause: String }
  | AnchoredBindingAnchorNotForRow { cause: String }
  | AnchoredBindingAnchorAbsent { cause: String }
  | AnchoredBindingPresentedKeyMismatch { expected_line: String, observed_line: String }
  | AnchoredBindingPinFromAnotherBoot { pinned_boot: String, expected_boot: String }
  | AnchoredBindingRefused { cause: String }

// THE BOUNDING, generic over the anchored machine; every refusal a typed, located state (§5). The host
// is NOT an input: it is read from the transport by host_bound_transport_of -- the same route a FleetSsh
// target is built by -- so no caller can pair a transport to one machine with the trust of another (the
// wrong-host guarantee the re-land made structural). The checks happen in this order:
//   1. host_bound_transport_of does the HOST binding. Its refusals pass through whole -- LocalShell,
//      SshShell, EmitArtifactThenThinRun, an unmanaged address, an ambiguous address all refuse there.
//      This module adds no second host list and no second spelling of an address (§3).
//   2. The bound host MUST have a row. A machine with no row is not anchored -- a refusal that says so;
//      there is no fallback path that proceeds unanchored.
//   3. A row whose anchor is absent (the honest production state today) refuses carrying the read
//      obligation: matching against nothing is accepting anything.
//   4. The ANCHOR MUST STAND FOR THE ROW IT IS COMPARED AGAINST: the anchor carries its own host and
//      address (KnownHostKeyRow), and if either disagrees with the row's, a trust statement about one
//      machine has been paired with the row of another -- the wrong-pairing defect the re-land closed at
//      the host layer, now one layer lower. It is checked INSIDE the sealed comparison, so identity is
//      structural, not convention: no caller, admitted or not, can hand an anchor for machine A into a
//      comparison under row B. The production wrapper passes the row's own anchor (consistent by
//      construction); the witness is admitted to hand in one, which is exactly where a mismatch is
//      writable -- pinned by its own RED.
//   5. The presented line must equal the anchor's known_hosts line exactly -- a key differing in any
//      position is a different key. The presented line is a SUPPLIED VALUE at this boundary (the
//      readback mints it on a live boot); the production route is the gated scan below, and the witness
//      boundary is admitted to the comparison directly, as in the re-land's witness precedent.
fn anchored_host_transport_of(transport: HostEffectTransport, presented_key_line: String) -> AnchoredHostBinding {
  match host_bound_transport_of(transport: transport) {
    HostBoundTransportRefused { cause: cause } => AnchoredBindingRefused { cause: cause }
    HostBoundTransportResolved { bound: bound } => match anchored_host_row_for(host: bound.host) {
      Absent => AnchoredBindingAnchorAbsent {
        cause: join(["no anchored row exists for ", bound.host as String, "; a transport is only host-authenticated against a trusted statement of its host's key"], ""),
      }
      Present { value: row } => match row.anchor {
        Absent => AnchoredBindingAnchorAbsent {
          cause: join([
            "no trusted statement about ", bound.host as String, "'s host key exists: the stable key (secret name ",
            row.host_key_secret.secret as String,
            ") has not been minted and its public half transcribed. Read obligation: ",
            row.read_obligation as String,
          ], ""),
        }
        Present { value: anchor } => anchored_host_transport_against(row: row, anchor: anchor, transport: transport, presented_key_line: presented_key_line)
      }
    }
  }
}

// The comparison against a GIVEN anchor, sealed to one constructor for the family: the production wrapper
// above supplies the production row and anchor, and the witness is admitted to supply fixture ones -- the
// same boundary shape the re-land's witness uses (hand in the read, call the join).
fn anchored_host_transport_against(
  row: AnchoredHostRow,
  anchor: KnownHostKeyRow,
  transport: HostEffectTransport,
  presented_key_line: String,
) -> AnchoredHostBinding
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.host.anchored_host_transport", decl_name: "anchored_host_transport_of"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.host.anchored_host_transport", decl_name: "anchored_host_transport_per_boot"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.host.anchored_host_transport_witness", decl_name: "a_wrong_presented_key_refuses_the_transport"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.host.anchored_host_transport_witness", decl_name: "matching_presented_key_binds_the_anchored_host"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.host.anchored_host_transport_witness", decl_name: "a_transport_to_another_machine_never_binds_the_anchored_host"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.host.anchored_host_transport_witness", decl_name: "a_local_shell_refuses_before_any_key_is_read"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.host.anchored_host_transport_witness", decl_name: "an_empty_presented_line_never_binds"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.host.anchored_host_transport_witness", decl_name: "an_anchor_for_another_machine_refuses_the_row"),
  ] {
  match host_bound_transport_of(transport: transport) {
    HostBoundTransportRefused { cause: cause } => AnchoredBindingRefused { cause: cause }
    HostBoundTransportResolved { bound: bound } =>
      if host_identity_eq(a: bound.host, b: row.host) {
        if !host_identity_eq(a: anchor.host, b: row.host) || anchor.address != row.address {
          // The trust statement names a different machine (or a different endpoint) than the row it is
          // being compared under. Compared anyway, it would let an anchor authored for A vouch for B's
          // row -- the wrong-pairing defect, one layer below the host binding the re-land closed.
          AnchoredBindingAnchorNotForRow {
            cause: join([
              "the anchor statement names ", anchor.host as String, " at ",
              render_network_host(host: anchor.address.host) as String,
              "; the row is the trust record of ", row.host as String,
              "; an anchor is admitted only for the machine and endpoint its row names, and pairing them is refused"], ""),
          }
        } else {
          let expected = known_hosts_line(k: anchor)
          if expected == presented_key_line {
            AnchoredBindingBound { bound: bound }
          } else {
            AnchoredBindingPresentedKeyMismatch { expected_line: expected, observed_line: presented_key_line }
          }
        }
      } else {
        AnchoredBindingNotTheAnchoredHost {
          cause: join(["the transport bound to ", bound.host as String, ", not to ", row.host as String, "; an anchored binding binds its anchored host and nothing else"], ""),
        }
      }
  }
}

// ── 2b. THE PER-BOOT PIN (operator-delegated route, merry-fox-82 2026-10-31) ─────────────────────────
//
// mtcollins1's runner OS is a RAM image: a stable host key cannot reach it before sshd starts (the custody
// arm delivers over the very SSH it would have to start). The key is therefore generated ON the host at
// every boot and the image prints its PUBLIC line on the BMC serial console (SOL), which is authenticated
// by the BMC credential and independent of the network path under test. No secret crosses any channel.
// What the fleet pins is that line, TIED TO THE BOOT it was printed in: a pin from another boot is a pin
// for another key, so the boot id is part of the pin and compared before the key is.
//
// The comparison is unchanged -- anchored_host_transport_against, the known_hosts-line equality -- so a
// per-boot pin is one more source of an anchor, not a second trust algorithm (§3).
type PerBootHostPin {
  boot_id: NonEmptyStr
  anchor: KnownHostKeyRow
}

// THE CONSOLE LINE THE IMAGE PRINTS: `GUNBC-HOST-KEY boot_id=<id> <key_type> <base64> <SHA256:fingerprint>`,
// five space-separated fields, a public key and nothing secret. Anything else is no pin: a malformed or
// truncated console read is an Absent pin and every transport refuses at AnchoredBindingAnchorAbsent,
// never a partial key.
data per_boot_console_marker: String = "GUNBC-HOST-KEY"

fn per_boot_pin_from_console_line(row: AnchoredHostRow, line: String) -> PerBootHostPin? {
  let fields = filter(split(s: trim(s: line), delimiter: " "), f => f != "")
  match fields |> skip(n: 5) |> first {
    Present { value: _ } => none
    Absent => per_boot_pin_from_fields(row: row, fields: fields)
  }
}

fn per_boot_pin_from_fields(row: AnchoredHostRow, fields: List<String>) -> PerBootHostPin? {
  match fields |> first {
    Absent => none
    Present { value: marker } => match fields |> skip(n: 1) |> first {
      Absent => none
      Present { value: boot_field } => match fields |> skip(n: 2) |> first {
        Absent => none
        Present { value: key_type } => match fields |> skip(n: 3) |> first {
          Absent => none
          Present { value: key_b64 } => match fields |> skip(n: 4) |> first {
            Absent => none
            Present { value: fingerprint } =>
              if marker == per_boot_console_marker && key_type == "ssh-ed25519" && starts_with_sha256(f: fingerprint) {
                per_boot_pin_of(row: row, boot_field: boot_field, key_type: key_type, key_b64: key_b64, fingerprint: fingerprint)
              } else { none }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

// "boot_id=a=b" is not "boot_id=a": a piece beyond the second is refused, never dropped (§5).
fn has_no_third_piece(s: String) -> Bool {
  match split(s: s, delimiter: "=") |> skip(n: 2) |> first {
    Absent => true
    Present { value: _ } => false
  }
}

fn per_boot_pin_of(row: AnchoredHostRow, boot_field: String, key_type: String, key_b64: String, fingerprint: String) -> PerBootHostPin? {
  match split(s: boot_field, delimiter: "=") |> first {
    Absent => none
    Present { value: tag } => match split(s: boot_field, delimiter: "=") |> skip(n: 1) |> first {
      Absent => none
      Present { value: id } =>
        if tag == "boot_id" && id != "" && has_no_third_piece(s: boot_field) {
          Present { value: PerBootHostPin {
            boot_id: id as NonEmptyStr,
            anchor: KnownHostKeyRow {
              host: row.host,
              address: row.address,
              key_type: key_type,
              public_key_base64: key_b64,
              sha256_fingerprint: fingerprint,
              provenance: ConsolePerBoot {
                boot_id: id as NonEmptyStr,
                channel: join(["the BMC serial console (SOL), printed by the image from the host key it generated at that boot; read obligation: ", row.read_obligation as String], "") as NonEmptyStr
              },
            },
          } }
        } else { none }
    }
  }
}

fn starts_with_sha256(f: String) -> Bool {
  match split(s: f, delimiter: ":") |> first {
    Present { value: head } => head == "SHA256"
    Absent => false
  }
}

// THE PER-BOOT BINDING. The pin is a SUPPLIED VALUE (the console read mints it); the expected boot id is
// the boot the caller is acting on (the subject's boot id), so a pin captured at boot A can never vouch
// for boot B's sshd. Order: no pin refuses; a pin from another boot refuses before any key is compared;
// then the same host binding and row lookup anchored_host_transport_of does, and the same sealed
// comparison against the pin's anchor.
fn anchored_host_transport_per_boot(
  transport: HostEffectTransport,
  expected_boot_id: NonEmptyStr,
  pin: PerBootHostPin?,
  presented_key_line: String,
) -> AnchoredHostBinding {
  match pin {
    Absent => AnchoredBindingAnchorAbsent {
      cause: "no per-boot host-key pin: the console read of this boot's key line is absent or malformed; matching against nothing is accepting anything",
    }
    Present { value: p } =>
      if (p.boot_id as String) != (expected_boot_id as String) {
        AnchoredBindingPinFromAnotherBoot { pinned_boot: p.boot_id as String, expected_boot: expected_boot_id as String }
      } else {
        match host_bound_transport_of(transport: transport) {
          HostBoundTransportRefused { cause: cause } => AnchoredBindingRefused { cause: cause }
          HostBoundTransportResolved { bound: bound } => match anchored_host_row_for(host: bound.host) {
            Absent => AnchoredBindingAnchorAbsent {
              cause: join(["no anchored row exists for ", bound.host as String], ""),
            }
            Present { value: row } => anchored_host_transport_against(row: row, anchor: p.anchor, transport: transport, presented_key_line: presented_key_line)
          }
        }
      }
  }
}

// The refusal text, kept beside the coproduct so no consumer invents wording for a state the model names
// (the fleet_ssh_credential_verify refusal-reason pattern). A bound transport is not a refusal and says
// so; no arm's text can carry key material, because no arm carries any field that could hold one beyond
// the PRESENTED and EXPECTED PUBLIC lines OpenSSH would print anyway.
fn anchored_host_binding_refusal_reason(b: AnchoredHostBinding) -> String {
  match b {
    AnchoredBindingBound { bound: _ } => "bound; not a refusal"
    AnchoredBindingNotTheAnchoredHost { cause: cause } => cause
    AnchoredBindingAnchorNotForRow { cause: cause } => cause
    AnchoredBindingAnchorAbsent { cause: cause } => cause
    AnchoredBindingPresentedKeyMismatch { expected_line: expected, observed_line: observed } =>
      join(["AnchoredBindingPresentedKeyMismatch: got `", observed as String, "`, not the anchored key `", expected as String, "`; contacting NO host"], "")
    AnchoredBindingPinFromAnotherBoot { pinned_boot: pinned, expected_boot: expected } =>
      join(["the pin was printed at boot ", pinned, ", not boot ", expected, "; a per-boot key vouches for its own boot only"], "")
    AnchoredBindingRefused { cause: cause } => cause
  }
}

// ── 3. The scan's credential: EXECUTED out of the selectors; typed outputs cited, never hand-picked ─

// THE OPERATOR GO IS A HUMAN INTERVENTION, not a flag read. The scan reaches a live host's sshd and reads
// the run's access token source to authorize itself; what stands behind it is the named human decision
// (for mtcollins1: merry-fox-82's go, relayed by snappy-koi-83), carried as a value the way every other
// irreversible or gated effect in the fleet carries its human (the AC power cycle row, the WIF binding
// row). The environment variable below is the DISPATCH SURFACE of that decision, never a substitute for
// it: no workflow or dispatch supplies the variable, and the wet arm says out loud that a Present value
// without the relayed go is out-of-model.
fn anchored_host_key_readback_go_step(host: HostIdentity) -> HumanIntervention {
  HumanIntervention {
    identity: concat("anchored_host_key_readback_go_", host as String) as HumanInterventionIdentity,
    frequency: FleetOnce,
    subject: "the one readback scan that discharges the anchor's read obligation on a live boot of this host" as NonEmptyStr,
    instruction: "on the booted host: run this module's anchored_host_key_scan_wet with GUNBC_HOST_KEY_READBACK_GO present (the operator go for mtcollins1 comes from merry-fox-82, relayed by snappy-koi-83), and record the presented key through the real dispatch (gunbc.runner.runner_lost_boot_sweep_plan lost_boot_sweep_effect_pairing_frontier)" as NonEmptyStr,
    completion_evidence: NoDischargeSiteModeled,
  }
}

// THE SCAN'S CENSUS-CLASSIFIED EFFECT, one per anchored row. Read by gunbc.auth.privileged_effect_census
// and classified there at site gunbc.host.anchored_host_transport::anchored_host_key_scan_wet. It is
// built exactly as the census's own manual_no_api_effect builds one -- the direction of the import is
// census into the feature module (the AC power-cycle row's shape), so the effect is spelled from
// gunbc.auth.authorization_pattern_selection's own arms here. It is a manual step with no API surface --
// which is what the gated readback is: it runs when a human, holding the go, runs it -- so the fold
// selects HumanOnlyStep and the row realizes RealizedHumanStep, and conforms.
fn anchored_host_key_scan_effect(host: HostIdentity) -> PrivilegedEffect {
  let row_opt = anchored_host_row_for(host: host)
  let go = anchored_host_key_readback_go_step(host: host)
  match row_opt {
    Absent => PrivilegedEffect {
      subject: "run the gated host-key readback scan for a host that is not anchored: it contacts a live host's sshd at the standard port with ssh-keyscan (an anonymous read that offers no credential) and resolves the run's access token source to authorize the leg; the named human go is the human step, and no workflow dispatches this" as NonEmptyStr,
      frequency: go.frequency,
      reversibility: ReversibleByReapply,
      surface: HumanSurfaceOnly { step: go },
      workload_identity: WorkloadIdentityUnbindable { cause: "the leg is authorized by the named human go, not by a workload identity bound to a token exchange; ssh-keyscan itself authenticates nothing about the caller" as NonEmptyStr },
      minted_reach: MintsNoCredential,
      billing: NoBillingConsequence,
      witness_discharge: NoWitnessDischarge,
    }
    Present { value: row } => PrivilegedEffect {
      subject: join([
        "run the gated ", row.host as String, " host-key readback scan: contact ", row.host as String,
        "'s sshd at the standard port with ssh-keyscan (an anonymous read that offers no credential) and resolve the run's access token source to authorize the leg; the named human go (",
        row.host_key_secret.secret as String, " backs the anchor) is the human step, and no workflow dispatches this",
      ], "") as NonEmptyStr,
      frequency: go.frequency,
      reversibility: ReversibleByReapply,
      surface: HumanSurfaceOnly { step: go },
      workload_identity: WorkloadIdentityUnbindable { cause: "the leg is authorized by the named human go, not by a workload identity bound to a token exchange; ssh-keyscan itself authenticates nothing about the caller" as NonEmptyStr },
      minted_reach: MintsNoCredential,
      billing: NoBillingConsequence,
      witness_discharge: NoWitnessDischarge,
    }
  }
}

// THE PATTERN CITATION. select_authorization_pattern runs over the census-classified effect; its TYPED
// output -- pattern plus receipt, or the named refusal/need -- is carried into the scan's text verbatim,
// so what authorized (or refused) a leg is readable from the leg. Nothing here hand-picks a credential
// path; the pattern named by the fold, not chosen by this module, is what authorizes the scan leg.
fn anchored_host_pattern_citation(host: HostIdentity) -> String {
  match select_authorization_pattern(e: anchored_host_key_scan_effect(host: host)) {
    PatternSelected { pattern: _, receipt: _ } => "select_authorization_pattern: PatternSelected (the admissible pattern, with its selection receipt)"
    ManualStepRequired { step: _, receipt: _ } => "select_authorization_pattern: ManualStepRequired (authorization selected the human-only candidate: the relayed go is what stands behind this leg, with its receipt)"
    NoAdmissiblePattern { causes: causes, scope: _ } => join(["select_authorization_pattern: NoAdmissiblePattern causes=", join(map(causes, c => c as String), "; ")], "")
    PatternSelectionNeedsEvidence { needs: _ } => "select_authorization_pattern: PatternSelectionNeedsEvidence"
    PatternSelectionNeedsPolicy { survivors: _ } => "select_authorization_pattern: PatternSelectionNeedsPolicy"
    PatternSelectionRefused { defects: _ } => "select_authorization_pattern: PatternSelectionRefused"
  }
}

// THE TOKEN-SOURCE CITATION. select_access_token_source resolves the credential the leg would run under
// from the run's environment; its typed output is cited whole, never flattened to a bool.
fn anchored_host_token_source_citation() -> String {
  match select_access_token_source() {
    AccessTokenSourceSelected { source: _ } => "select_access_token_source: AccessTokenSourceSelected"
    AccessTokenSourceUnavailable { cause: cause } => join(["select_access_token_source: AccessTokenSourceUnavailable -- ", cause as String], "")
  }
}

// ── 4. The readback scan: PREPARED, GATED, and honest about what has not run ──────────────────────

// THE SCAN COMMAND, built by the SSH command route the enrollment registry itself uses (ssh_keyscan_command
// at ed25519), against the address the anchor is stated at -- one scanning route, one endpoint spelling.
// argv carries the HOST STRING ONLY: no secret, no key material, nothing that could carry the private
// half (rule Q1; the class in dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode/a_secret_crosses_into_shell_stdin_as_a_
// plain_string.dag -- argv is rendered wherever it runs, so what lands in argv is what gets read).
fn anchored_host_key_scan_command(row: AnchoredHostRow) -> ArgvCommand {
  ssh_keyscan_command(
    host: render_network_host(host: row.address.host) as String,
    key_type: "ed25519",
    timeout_seconds: 5,
  )
}

// argv AS TEXT, for the claim that pins it: program plus operands, the way it would cross to the
// runner. The witness asserts no rendered leg carries private material (the secret-crossing-argv class).
fn anchored_host_key_scan_argv_text(row: AnchoredHostRow) -> String {
  let cmd = anchored_host_key_scan_command(row: row)
  join(concat([cmd.program.invocation as String], cmd.arguments), " ")
}

// THE PREPARED, GATED READBACK -- the dry run the brief orders prepared and NOT run. It refuses unless
// the operator go variable GUNBC_HOST_KEY_READBACK_GO is present in the environment, and no workflow or
// dispatch supplies that variable: the live boot and this scan wait on merry-fox-82's go relayed by
// snappy-koi-83 (the lost-boot mode stays GATED the same way). When the go lands, the printed evidence is
// what discharges the anchor's read obligation, and recording it must go through the real dispatch
// (lost_boot_sweep_effect_pairing_frontier -- the pairing obligation #14738 left open). THE FRONTIER IS
// SAID, NOT HIDDEN: until a live boot runs, no executed evidence stands behind the anchor, and any
// transport routed through anchored_host_transport_of refuses at AnchoredBindingAnchorAbsent. Production
// does not route through it yet -- anchored_host_transport_frontier_rows carries that with its trigger.
fn anchored_host_key_scan_wet(host: HostIdentity) -> String {
  match anchored_host_row_for(host: host) {
    Absent => join(["scan refused: ", anchored_host_binding_refusal_reason(b: AnchoredBindingAnchorAbsent { cause: join(["no anchored row exists for ", host as String], "") }), "\n"], "")
    Present { value: row } => match shell.Env.Get(name: "GUNBC_HOST_KEY_READBACK_GO").value {
      Absent => join([
        "GATED: the ", row.host as String, " host-key readback does not run without GUNBC_HOST_KEY_READBACK_GO in the environment ",
        "(the operator go for the live boot and scan comes from merry-fox-82, relayed by snappy-koi-83); nothing contacted, nothing minted.\n",
        "prepared argv: ", anchored_host_key_scan_argv_text(row: row), "\n",
        "selectors cited -- ", anchored_host_pattern_citation(host: host), " | ", anchored_host_token_source_citation(), "\n",
      ], "")
      Present { value: _ } =>
        match run_shell_command_capture(command: anchored_host_key_scan_command(row: row), transport: LocalExec) {
          ProcessOutputPresent { text: key_text } => join([
            "scan host=", row.host as String, " outcome=observed\n",
            "presented ", trim(s: key_text), "\n",
            "record this presented line through the REAL dispatch (lost_boot_sweep_effect_pairing_frontier); ",
            "selectors cited -- ", anchored_host_pattern_citation(host: host), " | ", anchored_host_token_source_citation(), "\n",
          ], "")
          ProcessOutputAbsent => join(["scan host=", row.host as String, " outcome=no-key-offered; nothing to anchor-match\n"], "")
          ProcessRefused { exit_code: _, stderr: e } => join(["scan host=", row.host as String, " outcome=refused cause=", trim(s: e), "\n"], "")
        }
    }
  }
}

// ── THE LIVE ANCHORED TRANSPORT, ONE COMPOSITION FOR EVERY CALLER ───────────────────────────────
//
// A production fold that sends traffic to an anchored host gets its transport here and nowhere else
// (gunbc.plans.mtcollins1_ci_service_legs: the qualification driver G1b and the lost-boot sweep's dry run F4):
// the host's row; its anchor, with no network contact when there is none; the operator's go, the same gate
// anchored_host_key_scan_wet reads; the fleet SSH context prepared with THIS host's anchor as its only
// known-hosts row, so every SSH leg enforces the key; the presented key scanned; and anchored_host_transport_of
// over that FleetSsh transport and that line. Every refusal is a typed AnchoredHostBinding arm before any
// effect on the host, and only AnchoredBindingBound carries a transport.
fn anchored_host_transport_live(host: HostIdentity, attempt_raw: String) -> AnchoredHostBinding {
  match anchored_host_row_for(host: host) {
    Absent => AnchoredBindingAnchorAbsent { cause: join(["no anchored row exists for ", host as String], "") }
    Present { value: row } => match row.anchor {
      Absent => AnchoredBindingAnchorAbsent {
        cause: join(["no trusted statement about ", host as String, "'s host key exists; nothing contacted. Read obligation: ", row.read_obligation as String], ""),
      }
      Present { value: anchor } => anchored_host_transport_live_gated(host: host, row: row, anchor: anchor, attempt_raw: attempt_raw, basis: LiveStaticAnchor)
    }
  }
}

// THE PER-BOOT ROUTE, THE SAME COMPOSITION: the anchor is this boot's pin (read off the serial console by
// gunbc.runner.runner_host_medium runner_host_key_observation) rather than the row's static one, so a row with no
// stable anchor (mtcollins1) still gets a host-authenticated transport -- and only for the boot the pin names.
fn anchored_host_transport_live_per_boot(host: HostIdentity, attempt_raw: String, pin: PerBootHostPin, expected_boot_id: NonEmptyStr) -> AnchoredHostBinding {
  match anchored_host_row_for(host: host) {
    Absent => AnchoredBindingAnchorAbsent { cause: join(["no anchored row exists for ", host as String], "") }
    Present { value: row } => anchored_host_transport_live_gated(host: host, row: row, anchor: pin.anchor, attempt_raw: attempt_raw, basis: LivePerBootPin { pin: pin, expected_boot_id: expected_boot_id })
  }
}

type LiveBindingBasis
  = LiveStaticAnchor
  | LivePerBootPin { pin: PerBootHostPin, expected_boot_id: NonEmptyStr }

fn anchored_host_transport_live_gated(host: HostIdentity, row: AnchoredHostRow, anchor: KnownHostKeyRow, attempt_raw: String, basis: LiveBindingBasis) -> AnchoredHostBinding {
  match shell.Env.Get(name: "GUNBC_HOST_KEY_READBACK_GO").value {
    Absent => AnchoredBindingRefused {
      cause: join(["GATED: no live transport to ", host as String, " without GUNBC_HOST_KEY_READBACK_GO (the operator go relayed by merry-fox-82); nothing contacted"], ""),
    }
    Present { value: _ } => match prepare_ssh_agent_context(attempt_raw: attempt_raw, key: fleet_automation_ssh_key, fingerprint: fleet_automation_ssh_key_fingerprint as NonEmptyStr, rows: [anchor]) {
      FleetSshContextRefused { cause: c } => AnchoredBindingRefused { cause: c }
      FleetSshContextReady { context: context, receipt: _ } => match fleet_locus_ssh_target(host: host) {
        SshTargetRefused { endpoint: e, refusal: _ } => AnchoredBindingRefused { cause: join(["the fleet endpoint ", e, " for ", host as String, " is not an SSH target"], "") }
        SshTargetResolved { target: target } =>
          match run_shell_command_capture(command: anchored_host_key_scan_command(row: row), transport: LocalExec) {
            ProcessOutputPresent { text: key_text } => match basis {
              LiveStaticAnchor => anchored_host_transport_of(transport: FleetSsh { target: target, context: context }, presented_key_line: trim(s: key_text))
              LivePerBootPin { pin: p, expected_boot_id: b } => anchored_host_transport_per_boot(transport: FleetSsh { target: target, context: context }, expected_boot_id: b, pin: Present { value: p }, presented_key_line: trim(s: key_text))
            }
            ProcessOutputAbsent => AnchoredBindingRefused { cause: join([host as String, " offered no host key to the scan"], "") }
            ProcessRefused { exit_code: _, stderr: e } => AnchoredBindingRefused { cause: join(["the host-key scan of ", host as String, " was refused: ", trim(s: e)], "") }
          }
      }
    }
  }
}

// ── THE MINT THAT USED TO LIVE HERE, AND WHAT REPLACED IT ──────────────────────────────────────
//
// Until 2026-10-28 this module owned the mint of mtcollins1's stable SSH host key: a modeled human shell
// (anchored_host_key_mint_shell, emitted leg by leg through bash_emit_stmts), a modeled human step
// (anchored_host_key_mint_intervention), a privileged effect (anchored_host_key_mint_effect, IRREVERSIBLE
// with a loss named) and its own dissolution trigger (anchored_host_key_mint_shell_-
// emit_dissolution_trigger, which said: when orchestration-to-shell emission can build a compound statement
// list, including a trap, this scaffold is replaced by a fleet-converge workflow_dispatch input and the
// runbook's Step 1 is DELETED).
//
// The trigger fired, and the replacement is stronger than the trigger asked for. The trigger anticipated a
// SCRIPT the run emits and a human runs. What landed instead is a mint: one keypair-mint policy
// (gunbc.host.fleet_keypair_mint, delivered as its root design 6b demands -- ONE policy with a row per keypair
// rather than a second implementation of "the private half never leaves tmpfs") with two subjects,
// gunbc.host.boot_medium_reader_key_mint and gunbc.host.mtcollins1_ssh_host_key_mint. The operator's ruling is
// a design_ruling row, the_mint_of_a_fleet_ssh_keypair_is_account_creation ("i don't see why a human needs to
// do this - this seems just like normal account creation"), and the census row moved with it:
// gunbc.auth.privileged_effect_census now carries the mint at the new site with
// RealizedFederatedGrant, and the argument for why the SELECTION flipped from OperatorApprovedCapability to the
// federated grant -- that the irreversibility forcing a human's consent was a property of the human process
// rather than of the key -- is made once there, not here.
//
// WHAT CARRIED OVER, BECAUSE IT WAS THE PART THAT MATTERED. Every safety property of the retired scaffold is
// a property of the mint that replaced it, and none was re-derived from scratch:
//   - the tmpfs guard (the directory's filesystem is READ from findmnt and required to be tmpfs BEFORE
//     ssh-keygen runs, never assumed from a path string that a bind mount could betray);
//   - trap cleanup (the directory is removed on every path out of the generation, and a refusal that could
//     not remove a directory it created says so, because an existing directory's owner is the run that made
//     it and deleting somebody else's would destroy the evidence of an unaccounted key);
//   - the private half on stdin only, into AddVersion, base64'd -- never in argv where any process on a
//     self-hosted runner can read it, never in a log, never on a durable path. The argv RED is
//     dag/test/claim/host/fleet_keypair_mint_witness.dag; the Q1 RED is the tmpfs gate's;
//   - the verify-before-upload rule (a public line that is not one ssh-ed25519 key, or a fingerprint that is
//     not SHA256-shaped, refuses before anything is stored);
//   - BOTH PIN HALVES, IN ONE COMMIT -- which is why the new receipt carries the fingerprint rather than
//     leaving it to be transcribed by hand into this module's anchor row.
//
// WHAT IS GONE, AND WHY NOTHING MAY TAKE ITS PLACE: no script is emitted here, and no human pastes a mint for
// a fleet key. The minting identity's secretVersionAdder arrives as a row of
// gunbc.auth.fleet_secret_accessor_roster converged by gunbc.auth.gcp_iam_converge, never as a console edit --
// a hand-made grant is unmodeled authority that nothing lists, nothing revokes, and that would make this
// census a description of a fleet that does not exist. Dispatching the mint remains an OPERATOR GO.
//
// The anchor row above is untouched and still unskippable: a minted key with no anchor is a live credential
// nothing can prove it holds, and a transport that cannot verify the host it is connecting to has lost the
// only property that makes the connection mean anything.
